id: pm-ts-starter-schema-rehearsal
title: Rehearse extension item schema migrations without changing source trackers
description: "Repeatable extension-owned item-data rehearsal using SDK schema migration operations on an isolated copy, with resumable steps and field-level diagnostics."
type: Feature
status: in_progress
priority: 1
tags[1]: "gh:unbraind/pm-ts-starter#151"
created_at: "2026-10-23T19:59:52.634Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-23T21:02:27.772Z"
author: codex-agent
acceptance_criteria: An interrupted migration resumes once; Invalid old data yields field-level diagnostics; No original tracker is modified during rehearsal
comments[13]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-23T20:00:11.407Z",codex-agent,"Overlap rechecked: SDK schemaRenameField/schemaRenameType/runSchemaEvolutionMigration already own planning, collision checks, canonical item writes and durable transaction recovery. pm-presets upgrade owns settings/configuration. This feature adds an isolated data rehearsal and field diagnostics around those APIs, never a competing schema engine. Tracker search found no duplicate; backend conformance is separate."
  "2026-10-23T20:11:44.760Z",codex-agent,"Implemented typed SDK rehearsal and rehearse-schema command using core SDK schema migration operations, canonical item parsing, certified full lists, atomic checkpoints and SDK locks. Targeted contracts: 18 pass; rehearsal module measured 100% lines/branches/functions. Real public pm-review snapshot at 536af20d: 53 items, 112 files, 1877486 bytes; 2 steps, 44 affected item-operation pairs; replay unchanged; read-only source fingerprint f25019de926f51be6dd25de81335f088ca7ac2aee5ef50c6806892cb1c5495f7. First measured SDK rehearsal 4337 ms. Hard termination recovery retains the SDK 300-second lease; test simulates runtime lease expiry only."
  "2026-10-23T20:14:13.158Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert proof: disabled actual SDK writes by setting dryRun:true in executeRehearsal controls, then ran node --test --test-name-pattern old/new test/rehearsal.test.ts. Both real fixture regressions failed with legacy_ref/Experiment retained instead of external_ref/Investigation. Restored implementation and rebuilt. Installed packed CLI acceptance also passes against the read-only public tracker with Git absent from PATH. Command uses createPmCliExpectedError and native verification_errors for field diagnostics."
  "2026-10-23T20:16:54.764Z",codex-agent,"Final local acceptance: 19 targeted tests pass, rehearsal source 100% lines/branches/functions; typecheck, test typecheck, lint, docstring and zero-duplication gates pass. pm test --run --progress ran targeted tests/typecheck/lint: 3 commands passed, evidence recording intentionally disabled by existing project settings, so results are recorded here. Independent public export comparison: all 112 original files byte-identical, same file set, all source files read-only; 22 field + 22 type changes across 53 items. Local health has pre-existing installed pm-github host-version skew and generated fence drift; CI performs its own pinned extension installation and prepare step. No history repair or fence work performed."
  "2026-10-23T20:18:04.307Z",codex-agent,"Independent semantic verification completed on the public export: all 53 canonical item documents and bodies match after only the intended field/type renames and updated_at removal for comparison. SDK list rows enrich linked files/docs with workspace-dependent existence data, so canonical SDK item documents were used for the lossless comparison. No original SDK client was opened for rehearsal. The original file-set and byte comparison remains 112/112 unchanged."
  "2026-10-23T20:21:26.307Z",codex-agent,"Self-review added a pre-lock scratch scan, including runtime directories, so an existing scratch locks symlink cannot redirect SDK lock acquisition into the source. New regression passes; targeted suite is now 20 tests with 100% rehearsal lines/branches/functions. PR: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-ts-starter/pull/151. Initial CI health and committed-output checks passed on Node 22 and 26; full release gates are running. Separate legacy demo error-code gap is tracked by pm-ts-starter-native-refusal-codes."
  "2026-10-23T20:23:10.130Z",codex-agent,"CI run https://github.com/unbraind/pm-ts-starter/actions/runs/40018240786 passed at 05c6edf: npm and Bun release:check each passed 216 tests on both Node 22 and Node 26, 0 failed, full configured coverage 100% lines/branches/functions across 8 measured sources. Both matrix health checks and committed dist checks passed. Final storage hardening increases the targeted suite to 20 tests (all pass), with 3/3 linked pm commands passed again. Reverting only the pre-lock scratch scan makes the lock-directory alias regression fail; restored scan, rebuilt distribution, test typecheck/lint/zero-duplication pass. Final commit will receive the same CI matrix before handoff."
  "2026-10-23T20:36:05.777Z",codex-agent,"Review round: remote head b100c9b is current and contains main. Complete GraphQL review-thread enumeration returned zero threads; no CodeRabbit review body exists (review skipped). Blocking independent verdict reproduced by inspection: settings fallback can hide custom items. Plan: reject SDK settings/schema warnings, reconcile physical corpus, test SDK, harness and installed CLI entry points with malformed/partial configuration, bounded input, path aliases and concurrent runs, record behavioral revert proofs, then run unchanged npm and Bun release gates."
  "2026-10-23T20:42:32.406Z",codex-agent,"Implemented fail-closed settings metadata handling, raw field-definition integrity checks, physical corpus reconciliation, and validation before resumed mutations. Adversarial review also added bounded plan-file reads, scope/name checks, directory traversal budgets and flat local custom-folder guards. Added direct SDK, registered-command and installed-CLI scenarios, including concurrent callers and source-byte preservation. Valid schema representation probes exposed the existing SDK workspace-history conflict for out-of-band schema edits; tests now verify pre-mutation value validation without rewriting any history."
  "2026-10-23T20:47:26.279Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert proofs (each mutation applied only to production behavior in rehearsal.ts, with tests unchanged; restored afterward):\nsettings-fallback: node --test --test-name-pattern=\"invalid settings cannot\" test/rehearsal.test.ts -> exit 1; 1 failing of 1 checks.\nfield-integrity: node --test --test-name-pattern=\"malformed and partial schemas\" test/rehearsal.test.ts -> exit 1; 4 failing of 10 checks.\nphysical-corpus: node --test --test-name-pattern=\"unregistered and nested|hidden physical\" test/rehearsal.test.ts -> exit 1; 4 failing of 4 checks.\nresume-inspection: node --test --test-name-pattern=\"resuming validates scratch|resuming a smaller\" test/rehearsal.test.ts -> exit 1; 2 failing of 2 checks.\nplan-contract: node --test --test-name-pattern=\"plan entry points\" test/rehearsal.test.ts -> exit 1; 1 failing of 1 checks.\nplan-file-boundary: node --test --test-name-pattern=\"plan entry points\" test/rehearsal.test.ts -> exit 1; 1 failing of 1 checks.\nsnapshot-budget: node --test --test-name-pattern=\"snapshot traversal\" test/rehearsal.test.ts -> exit 1; 1 failing of 1 checks.\nitem-folder-boundary: node --test --test-name-pattern=\"custom item folders\" test/rehearsal.test.ts -> exit 1; 5 failing of 6 checks.\nThe blocking settings-fallback revert reproduces false success and fails the explicit invalid-settings regression. Physical-corpus reverts hide orphan/hidden documents; resume revert allows journal/history work before rejecting a shrunken corpus. All mutations restored; final baseline and full gates follow. No review threads were replied to or resolved."
  "2026-10-23T20:52:03.705Z",codex-agent,"Final self-review added normalized plan-path consistency: safety checks and the actual filesystem read now use the identical resolved path. Its regression covers a symlink followed by parent traversal. Repeated all previous behavioral revert checks after the test setup refactor: all 8 still fail when reverted. Additional ninth proof: node --test --test-name-pattern=\"plan reads\" test/rehearsal.test.ts -> exit 1, 1 failing of 1 check when only plan-file reads/stat use the unchecked spelling again. All mutations restored. Full npm gate before this final path guard passed 247 checks with configured 100% lines/branches/functions; final linked test and both full gates are rerun on the complete implementation."
  "2026-10-23T20:56:11.708Z",codex-agent,"Concurrent stress uncovered an initialization race: a competing caller could win the SDK lease after the creator made the work directory but before its first checkpoint, and then all callers could refuse. Existing checkpoint-free scratch directories now refuse before lease acquisition. Deterministic behavioral revert proof: node --test --test-name-pattern=\"initializing scratch\" test/rehearsal.test.ts fails 1/1 when only that pre-lock guard is removed, because a competing caller creates lock storage. All ten production-behavior revert mutations now fail as intended. Refreshed the generated merge fence with the pinned CLI. Clean-HOME strict pm health passes; inherited global extension skew is environment-only. The pre-existing historical-provenance advisory is already recorded under pm-ts-starter-n4ee and no history records were rewritten."
  "2026-10-23T21:02:26.636Z",codex-agent,"Final validation: linked npm run build && npm run build:test && node --test test/rehearsal.test.ts passed 52/52 checks (selected linked command 1/1). Ten repeated concurrency tests passed with 60 same-directory callers. Final npm run release:check and bun run release:check each passed 249/249 checks, 0 failures/skips/cancellations, configured 100% lines/branches/functions across 8 sources, unchanged thresholds; statements are not independently measured. Both gates used a fresh HOME plus GIT_CONFIG_GLOBAL=/dev/null and GIT_CONFIG_NOSYSTEM=1. Production audit: 0 vulnerabilities. Duplication: 0% across 24 sources; docstring gate: 12 files, 35 declarations. Build/test typechecks, pack dry run, changelog, publish-attestation and release-date checks passed. Clean-environment strict tracker health passed after generated merge-fence refresh. Initial unisolated coverage encountered inherited npm allow-scripts configuration; clean-environment full gates passed. The initialization concurrency assertion failure was fixed, not waived as host load. All ten behavioral revert proofs are retained above, with production restored and dist rebuilt. Review disposition: 0 GitHub review threads; CodeRabbit review skipped with no review body or Outside diff range findings available; independent settings-fallback blocker fixed, plus self-review safety defects. Existing legacy provenance advisory remains tracked by pm-ts-starter-n4ee. No new CLI/SDK issue filed, thread reply/resolution, mention, merge, release or publish. Item stays in progress for orchestrator verification; release claim next."
